    "title": "Folsom man arrested, booked on charges of indecent exposure - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Chris D. Johnson ,\n2 hours ago\n(FOX40.COM) — Folsom Police arrested a man on charges of indecent exposure at multiple local businesses, the Folsom Police Department announced Wednesday.\nAccording to officials, 34-year-old Clifford Robinson was reported to have engaged in “lewd conduct” inside the Barnes & Noble store at the Palladio on Aug. 1. During the investigation, it was found that Robinson was involved in a similar incident on the same day at Sun & Shade in Folsom.\nRobinson was arrested on Tuesday and booked into the Sacramento County Main Jail on suspicion of felony indecent exposure as well as additional misdemeanor charges, officials said. His bail was set at $350,000.\nClifford Robinson\n(Photo: Folsom PD) Detectives investigating the case believe there may be additional victims. Anyone who had contact with Robinson at the Palladio on Aug. 1 and believes they may be a victim is encouraged to email Detective Joseph Howard via email at jhoward@folsom.ca.us .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX40 News.\n1",
    "summary": "By Chris D. Johnson , (FOX40.COM) — Folsom Police arrested a man on charges of indecent exposure at multiple local businesses, the Folsom Police Department announced Wednesday. According to officials, 34-year-old Clifford Robinson was reported to have engaged in “lewd conduct” inside the Barnes & Noble store at the Palladio on Aug. 1. During the investigation, it was found that Robinson was involved in a similar incident on the same day at Sun & Shade in Folsom.",
